==Special Moves==
===Ko'ou Ken===
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Ko'ou Ken
|moveId=marco_236A,marco_236C,marco_236AC
|input=236P
|description3=  

Classic fireball. Important part of Marco's neutral game. Marco's travel relatively fast, making them primarily useful for zoning and checking movement; not so much starting offense. The fireball appears around Marco's hand, so if you want better advantage on hit or block than listed, the opponent must be spaced somewhere in front of Marco's hand. Because of this, it's not the best cancel on block, however, the A version frame traps from lights and the C version frame traps from heavies, which can be useful. Unfortunately, even if they counter hit, you are too far away to get a conversion.

The AC version acts as a close range hit instead of a projectile, causing a launch. Its primary use is to be cancelled into 214AC to dash forward. On hit you get to continue the combo. On block Marco is left +3, allowing him to extend his pressure. Cancelling this from C normals is a frame trap, and if it counter hits, Marco is able to continue the juggle without cancelling into 214AC.

}}

===Kohou===
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Kohou
|moveId=marco_623A,marco_623C,marco_623C~AB,marco_623AC,marco_623AC~AB
|input=623P
|description5=  
() = damage value if the attack hits high up (outside of brake range)

Classic uppercut.

A version is fast and fully invincible. Use this as your meterless reversal.

C version has upper body invincibility making it great as an anti-air. When braked (which you have no good reason not to, ever), this acts as a safe on block combo starter as well. leading into great damage anywhere on screen. Its speed makes it easy to combo into from any normal, although the short horizontal range may make it whiff at some ranges.

The AC version acts almost identically to the C version but starts up one frame faster and can be used to extend juggles after 623C>Brake has already been used. It also launches slightly higher.

When the C and AC versions counter hit, the opponent gets launched very high in the air, allowing Marco to dash up and use the same uppercut again.

}}

===Hien Shippuu Kyaku===
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Hien Shippuu Kyaku
|moveId=marco_236B,marco_236B~AB,marco_236D,marco_236D~AB,marco_236BD,marco_236BD~AB
|input=236K
|description6=  

A series of flying kicks. 

The B version is a forward advancing flying kick that leads into a short combo on hit. Fast and combos reliably from all light normals except far A. Works well as a juggle ender as well. Can be used as a jump scare in neutral; works well against people who hop a lot, but is unsafe if blocked on the ground. This move can be braked before the kick connects, making the move act as a sort of dash. Note that if the opponent is too close (a little shorter than round start distance), the kick will automatically come out and it won't be able to be braked.

The D version is an upward knee followed by a downwards kick. Combo filler mainly. When braked, Marco skips the downward kick and recovers faster, allowing for juggles. This combos from 2A at all ranges but only connects on standing opponents. 2C forces stand, so hit confirms from that normal are guaranteed.

The BD version looks similar to the B version, but is faster and applies a hard knockdown. The corner carry and hard knockdown is very good for Marco, making this your preferred combo ender. Combos reliably from all lights, including far A. You can brake in the middle of the kicking animation, skipping the last kick. On block this leaves you at only -2, making this a useful neutral skip option. You can also use the brake version for some corner juggle extensions.
|display=150x150px
}}

===Hari Uke===
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Hari Uke
|moveId=marco_214A,marco_214C,marco_214AC
|input=214P
|description3=  
* Counter window is active at frame 3 (needs testing)
* Does not work against projectiles. 
* A and AC version counters highs and mids. C version counters lows.

A dash that triggers a counter if Marco gets hit during it. Can be used to make your opponent second guess their buttons, but this is very risky as it leaves Marco wide open to an easy Wild Punish combo if it doesn't work. Particularly useful against Rev Blows; if you are doing a normal and you confirm that they are armoring it with a Rev Blow, cancelling into the A version will counter the Rev Blow with a counter hit, which allows for a juggle combo. Note that since different characters have different start-up times for their Rev Blow, the timing will always be slightly different.

The AC version can be cancelled into other Rev Arts on a successful counter, notably 623AC > Brake, allowing for further damage. Note that on counter hit you do not get a special launch. It can also be cancelled into from 236AC to get juggles on hit and plus frames on block. This is an expensive but powerful option.
}}

===Ryuusen Ken===
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Ryuusen Ken
|moveId=marco_[P],marco_[AC]
|input=[P] then ]P[
|description2=  
* Button must be held for at least 60 frames.
* Often referred to as either "TAP" or "Zonk" by the community after the similar hold-then-release moves of Street Fighter's Boxer and Cody respectively.

Lunge punch. In order to use this, you must hold one or both of the punch buttons to charge it, then release to execute the move, which means sacrificing a few of your most important buttons and universal options such as throw or dodge at any given time. The move itself is a straightforward strike with not that much reward, so this move is rarely used outside of some optimized combos.

The AC version is notable for being plus on block. On its own, it doesn't leave Marco at a range where he can realistically threaten with much, however, Accel chaining it into 214AC retains the +4 block advantage and leaves Marco point blank. 
}}

